msgid "**New APIs**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:40
msgid ""
":gh:`3102`, :label:`breaking`: new :func:`memory_physical` "
"and :func:`memory_swap` functions. :func:`virtual_memory` "
"and :func:`swap_memory` still work, but are :term:`soft deprecated`. "
"See :ref:`migration guide <migration-8.0-memory-names>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:44
msgid ""
":gh:`2798`, :label:`breaking`: new :attr:`Process.attrs` class attribute, "
"a :class:`frozenset` of the attribute names accepted "
"by :meth:`Process.as_dict` and :func:`process_iter`. Passing ``attrs=[]`` "
"to :func:`process_iter` to mean \"retrieve all attributes\" is deprecated. "
"See :ref:`migration guide <migration-8.0-attrs>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:49
msgid ""
":gh:`2776`, [Windows], :label:`breaking`: :func:`virtual_memory` now "
"includes :field:`cached` and :field:`wired` fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:51
msgid ""
":gh:`3052`: new :attr:`Process.snapshot` attribute, a read-"
"only :class:`ProcessSnapshot` exposing the attributes collected "
"by :func:`process_iter` (``p.snapshot.name`` instead of "
"``p.info[\"name\"]``). ``Process.info`` still works but "
"raises :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. See :ref:`migration guide <migration-8.0-"
"snapshot>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:56
msgid ""
":gh:`1541`: new :meth:`Process.page_faults` method, returning a ``(minor, "
"major)`` named tuple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:58
msgid ""
":gh:`2780`, [Windows]: :func:`disk_usage` now accepts a file path, not only "
"a directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:60
msgid ""
":gh:`2816`, [OpenBSD]: :func:`swap_memory` :field:`sin` and :field:`sout` "
"are no longer set to ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:62
msgid ""
":gh:`3023`, [FreeBSD], [OpenBSD]: :func:`net_io_counters` :field:`dropout` "
"is no longer always ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:64
msgid ""
":gh:`3119`, [Windows]: :func:`cpu_stats` :field:`soft_interrupts` is no "
"longer always ``0``. It's the number of deferred procedure calls (DPCs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:66
msgid ""
":gh:`3120`, [Windows]: :func:`net_if_stats` :field:`duplex` is no longer "
"always :data:`NIC_DUPLEX_FULL`. It's now read from the NIC driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:68
msgid ""
":gh:`2977`: new :func:`bytes2human` function, converting bytes to a human-"
"readable string (e.g. ``9.8K``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:70
msgid ""
":gh:`1109`, [Linux]: :meth:`Process.memory_extras` returns a "
"new :field:`locked` field: locked virtual memory (:manpage:`mlock(2)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:72
msgid ""
":gh:`1452`, :gh:`2993`, [Linux], [macOS], "
"[Windows]: :meth:`Process.memory_footprint` returns a new :field:`shared` "
"field: resident memory shared with other processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:75
msgid ""
":gh:`3100`, [Linux], [SunOS], [AIX]: new :func:`set_procfs_path` function to "
"relocate ``/proc``, and :data:`PROCFS_PATH` now defaults to "
"the :envvar:`PSUTIL_PROCFS_PATH` environment variable when set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:79
msgid ""
"Reorganization of process memory APIs "
"(:gh:`2731`, :gh:`2736`, :gh:`2733`, :gh:`2988`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:82
msgid ""
"New :meth:`Process.memory_extras` method, returning extra platform-specific "
"memory metrics on Linux, macOS and Windows. See :ref:`migration guide "
"<migration-8.0-memory-extras>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:86
msgid ""
"New :meth:`Process.memory_footprint` method, "
"returning :field:`uss`, :field:`pss` and :field:`swap` "
"(what :meth:`Process.memory_full_info` used to return)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:90
msgid ""
":label:`breaking`: :meth:`Process.memory_full_info` is deprecated. Use the "
"new :meth:`Process.memory_footprint` instead. See :ref:`migration guide "
"<migration-8.0-memory-full-info>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:94
msgid ""
":label:`breaking`: :meth:`Process.memory_info` named tuple changed on all "
"platforms: fields were added, removed and renamed. Most old names still work "
"but raise :exc:`DeprecationWarning`; on macOS :field:`pfaults` "
"and :field:`pageins` were removed with **no backward-compatible aliases**, "
"use :meth:`Process.page_faults` instead. See :ref:`migration guide "
"<migration-8.0-namedtuples>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:101
msgid "**Type hints and enums**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:103
msgid ""
":gh:`2753`, :label:`breaking`: new enum classes "
"(:class:`ProcessStatus`, :class:`ConnectionStatus`, :class:`ProcessIOPriority`, :class:`ProcessPriority`, :class:`ProcessRlimit`) "
"grouping related constants. The top-level constants "
"(e.g. :data:`STATUS_RUNNING`) remain the primary API, and are now aliases of "
"the enum members. See :ref:`migration guide <migration-8.0-enums>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:109
msgid ""
":gh:`1946`: add inline type hints to all public APIs. mypy still relies on "
"the ``types-psutil`` stubs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:111
msgid ""
":gh:`2751`: named tuples are now :class:`typing.NamedTuple` classes with "
"type annotations, instead of :func:`collections.namedtuple`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:114
msgid "**Other API changes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:116
msgid ""
":gh:`2747`, :label:`breaking`: the :func:`cpu_times` field order is now the "
"same on all platforms, starting "
"with :field:`user`, :field:`system`, :field:`idle`. See :ref:`migration "
"guide <migration-8.0-namedtuples>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:119
msgid ""
":gh:`2772`, "
"[Windows], :label:`breaking`: :func:`cpu_times` :field:`interrupt` field "
"renamed to :field:`irq`, as on Linux and BSD. :field:`interrupt` still works "
"but raises :exc:`DeprecationWarning`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:122
msgid ""
":gh:`2889`, [Windows], :label:`breaking`: 32-bit psutil can no longer "
"inspect 64-bit processes: :meth:`Process.cwd` raises :exc:`AccessDenied` "
"(:meth:`Process.cmdline` and :meth:`Process.environ` are unaffected). 32-bit "
"wheels were already dropped in 7.1.2 (:gh:`2657`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:126
msgid ""
":gh:`2992`: :meth:`Process.memory_percent` is now rounded to 2 decimal "
"places, like the other ``*_percent`` APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:128
msgid ""
":gh:`2754`: :func:`sensors_battery` :field:`percent` is now a ``float`` on "
"all systems, not only Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:130
msgid ""
":gh:`2799`: :meth:`Process.as_dict` now returns a dict with keys sorted "
"alphabetically when *attrs* is not specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:132
msgid ""
":gh:`2805`, [BSD]: on NetBSD, :func:`cpu_stats` and :func:`memory_physical` "
"no longer depend on ``procfs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:134
msgid ""
":gh:`2947`: psutil now emits a :exc:`RuntimeWarning` when it returns "
"incomplete or approximated results (e.g. a failed sanity check on kernel "
"data). Before, these were only visible with :envvar:`PSUTIL_DEBUG`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:137
msgid ""
":gh:`3113`: :meth:`Process.connections` now raises :exc:`FutureWarning`, and "
"will be removed in 9.0. See :ref:`migration guide <migration-8.0-"
"connections>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:141 ../../../changelog.rst:596
#: ../../../changelog.rst:613 ../../../changelog.rst:679
