#: ../../../changelog.rst:3362
msgid "**Performance**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:152
msgid ""
":gh:`2695`, [Windows]: :func:`net_io_counters` is **~5x "
"faster**. :func:`net_if_stats` and :func:`net_if_addrs` also got faster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:154
msgid ""
":gh:`2919`, :gh:`2920`, [Windows]: :meth:`Process.threads` is around **25x "
"faster**, :meth:`Process.ppid` and :meth:`Process.children` around "
"3.5x. :meth:`Process.threads` also no longer silently misses the threads "
"which could not be opened due to :exc:`AccessDenied`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:158
msgid ""
":gh:`2922`, [Windows]: :meth:`Process.ppid` is around **58x faster** "
"(**99x** on ARM64)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:160
msgid ""
":gh:`2923`, [Windows]: :meth:`Process.status` is now part of "
"the :meth:`Process.oneshot` group. Reading 4 methods of that group in "
"one :meth:`Process.oneshot` block is now around **3.9x faster** than without "
"it, up from 2x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:164
msgid ""
":gh:`2932`, [Windows]: :meth:`Process.open_files` is **140x to 400x faster** "
"(from 235 ms to 0.39 ms per call)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:166
msgid ""
":gh:`2939`: syscalls which can block (disk devices, mount points, NIC "
"drivers, etc) now release the GIL, so a slow psutil call no longer freezes "
"the other threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:170 ../../../changelog.rst:533
#: ../../../changelog.rst:576 ../../../changelog.rst:618
#: ../../../changelog.rst:760 ../../../changelog.rst:934
#: ../../../changelog.rst:952 ../../../changelog.rst:1095
