msgid "**Internals**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:235
msgid ""
":gh:`2765`: add a PR bot that uses Claude to update ``changelog.rst`` and "
"``credits.rst`` when commenting with /changelog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:237
msgid ""
":gh:`2927`: Python dependencies are now installed with ``uv`` when "
"available, saving ~10 secs per CI run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:239
msgid ""
":gh:`3066`: the C extension is now compiled with ``-Wall -Wextra`` (``/W4`` "
"on Windows), with warnings as errors in CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:242
msgid "**Bug fixes: cross-platform**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:244
msgid ""
":gh:`2857`, [Linux], [SunOS], :label:`memleak`: :func:`disk_partitions` "
"(Linux) and :meth:`Process.environ` (SunOS) leaked a reference when argument "
"parsing failed. On SunOS :meth:`Process.environ` also checked the wrong "
"variable for NULL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:248
msgid ":gh:`2793`: :func:`process_iter` silently skipped zombie processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:249
msgid ""
":gh:`2830`, [Linux], [macOS], [BSD]: :meth:`Process.terminal` returned "
"``None`` for terminals opened after the first call (e.g. a new ``/dev/pts/"
"N``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:252
msgid ""
":gh:`2895`: :class:`Process` methods could wrongly "
"raise :exc:`NoSuchProcess` (\"PID has been reused\") when the process "
"creation time could not be determined (e.g. zombies on NetBSD / "
"OpenBSD, :exc:`AccessDenied` on Windows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:256
msgid ""
":gh:`2899`: two :class:`Process` instances for the same process could "
"compare unequal if the creation time could not be determined. "
"``hash(Process)`` is now based on the PID alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:260
msgid "**Bug fixes: Linux**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:262
msgid ""
":gh:`2860`, :gh:`2966`, :label:`critical`: :meth:`Process.cpu_affinity` "
"could segfault under memory pressure, and on Python <= 3.11 it corrupted "
"CPython's small integer cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:265
msgid ""
":gh:`2628`: :func:`cpu_freq` counted offline CPUs, reported with all-zero "
"frequencies, which dragged down the averages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:267
msgid ""
":gh:`2715`: :meth:`Process.wait` could fail with ``EINVAL`` due to a kernel "
"race condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:269
msgid ""
":gh:`2732`: :func:`net_if_stats` didn't handle ``EBUSY`` from "
"``ioctl(SIOCETHTOOL)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:271
msgid ""
":gh:`2770`: :func:`cpu_count` (``logical=False``) raised :exc:`ValueError` "
"on s390x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:273
msgid ""
":gh:`2809`: :func:`memory_swap` and :func:`memory_physical` "
"raised :exc:`ValueError` on arm64 when a :proc:`/proc/meminfo` field had no "
"space after the colon (e.g. ``ShadowCallStack:10373888 kB``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:276
msgid ""
":gh:`2967`: :func:`cpu_freq` returned ``None`` on ppc machines without "
"cpufreq sysfs, and reported twice as many CPUs on s390x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:278
msgid ""
":gh:`2512`: :func:`cpu_freq` with ``percpu=True`` returned one entry per "
"cpufreq policy instead of one per CPU (fewer entries than :func:`cpu_count` "
"on POWER9, Apple M1, RISC-V)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:281
msgid ""
":gh:`2611`: re-enable Android support, broken on Python "
"3.13. :func:`disk_partitions` no longer raises :exc:`PermissionError` there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:283
msgid ""
":gh:`3082`: :meth:`Process.cmdline` and :meth:`Process.environ` turned "
"``\\r`` and ``\\r\\n`` into ``\\n`` inside arguments and environment "
"variable values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:285
msgid ""
":gh:`3084`: :func:`disk_partitions` could return mixed-up entries when "
"called from multiple threads on free-threaded Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:287
msgid ""
":gh:`2347`: :func:`disk_partitions` gave ``/dev/root`` mounts the device of "
"``/``, which is a different one inside a chroot (e.g. a host directory bind "
"mounted into it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:290
msgid ""
":gh:`3110`: on Python 3.15+ :data:`RLIM_INFINITY` is now ``2**64-1``, "
"like :data:`resource.RLIM_INFINITY`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:293
msgid "**Bug fixes: Windows**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:295
msgid ""
":gh:`1967`, :label:`critical`: :meth:`Process.open_files` could deadlock the "
"calling process when a handle name query timed out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:297
msgid ""
":gh:`2859`, :label:`critical`: :func:`net_connections` / :meth:`Process.net_connections` "
"could crash when argument parsing failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:299
msgid ""
":gh:`2847`, :label:`critical`: :func:`cpu_stats` read the context switches "
"and syscalls counts from a buffer it had just freed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:301
msgid ""
":gh:`2934`, :label:`critical`: :meth:`Process.memory_maps` could crash with "
"a stack buffer overflow on mapped file paths longer than 260 characters. "
"Such paths are also no longer truncated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:304
msgid ""
":gh:`2937`, :label:`critical`: :func:`disk_io_counters` could let a disk "
"driver write past the end of a stack buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:306
msgid ""
":gh:`2943`, :label:`critical`: :func:`win_service_iter` could crash the "
"interpreter if the service enumeration failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:308
msgid ""
":gh:`2946`, :label:`critical`: :func:`heap_info` could read uninitialized "
"memory and return bogus values if the number of process heaps changed mid-"
"call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:311
msgid ""
":gh:`2972`, :label:`critical`: on systems with more than 64 "
"CPUs, :func:`cpu_times` (``percpu=True``) and :func:`cpu_stats` read "
"uninitialized memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:314
msgid ""
":gh:`2932`, :label:`memleak`: :meth:`Process.open_files` leaked a thread and "
"a handle for every name query which timed out, and could hang for ~1 minute "
"on files open on an unreachable network share."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:317
msgid ""
":gh:`2935`, :label:`memleak`: :meth:`Process.kill` "
"and :meth:`Process.terminate` leaked a process handle when "
"``TerminateProcess()`` failed with an error other than "
"``ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:320
msgid ""
":gh:`1007`: :func:`boot_time` fluctuated by ~1 second across calls and "
"processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:322
msgid ""
":gh:`1959`: :func:`disk_partitions` could raise :exc:`UnicodeDecodeError` on "
"non-UTF-8 ANSI code pages (e.g. cp1251)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:324
msgid ""
":gh:`1986`: :func:`disk_partitions` listed volumes mounted in a folder (e.g. "
"``C:\\mnt\\data``) only when running as administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:326
msgid ""
":gh:`2383`: :meth:`WindowsService.description` "
"(and :meth:`WindowsService.as_dict`) could fail with "
"``ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND`` when the description points to a missing resource "
"(e.g. ``WaaSMedicSvc``). It now returns an empty string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:330
msgid ""
":gh:`2655`: :func:`net_if_stats` returned ``4294967295`` as the speed of "
"NICs faster than ~4.29 Gbps (32-bit overflow)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:332
msgid ""
":gh:`2711`, :gh:`2940`: :func:`net_if_addrs` returned ``None`` "
"for :field:`broadcast`, and could report an IPv4 :field:`netmask` for an "
"IPv6 address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:335
msgid ""
":gh:`2875`: :func:`sensors_battery` returned ``4294967295`` instead "
"of :data:`POWER_TIME_UNKNOWN` when the remaining time was unknown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:337
msgid ""
":gh:`2938`: :func:`disk_partitions` :field:`opts` lacked the drive type "
"(``fixed``, ``cdrom``, ...) for volume mount points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:339
msgid ""
":gh:`2941`: :func:`net_io_counters` raised :exc:`RuntimeError` if a NIC was "
"disabled or unplugged mid-call. Now it's skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:341
msgid ""
":gh:`3002`: :func:`disk_io_counters` :field:`read_time` "
"and :field:`write_time` were in seconds instead of milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:343
msgid ""
":gh:`3016`: :meth:`Process.send_signal` with ``CTRL_C_EVENT`` or "
"``CTRL_BREAK_EVENT`` on PID 0 delivered the event to every process on the "
"caller's console, the caller included. It now raises :exc:`AccessDenied`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:346
msgid ""
":gh:`3019`: :meth:`Process.memory_maps` truncated :field:`rss` for regions "
"of 4 GiB or larger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:348
msgid ""
":gh:`3022`: :meth:`Process.wait` returned exit codes with the high bit set "
"(e.g. ``0xC0000005``) as negative numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:350
msgid ":gh:`3107`: :func:`disk_partitions` was not thread-safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:351
msgid ""
":gh:`3108`: :func:`disk_partitions` gave volumes mounted in a folder "
"the :field:`device`, :field:`fstype` and :field:`opts` of the drive holding "
"the folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:354
msgid ""
":gh:`3118`: :func:`memory_swap` returned a negative :field:`total` "
"and :field:`free` on systems with no page file. They are now ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:357
msgid "**Bug fixes: macOS**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:359
msgid ""
":gh:`2885`, :label:`critical`: :meth:`Process.memory_full_info`, :meth:`Process.memory_footprint` "
"and :meth:`Process.threads` could hang forever on headless VMs (e.g. CI "
"runners). They also raise :exc:`AccessDenied` less often."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:363
msgid ""
":gh:`2382`: :func:`cpu_freq` was undefined (or raised :exc:`RuntimeError`) "
"on virtualized ARM64 (e.g. CI runners). It now returns ``None`` when the "
"frequency can't be determined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:366
msgid ""
":gh:`2411`: :meth:`Process.cpu_times` and :meth:`Process.cpu_percent` were "
"~41x too low on x86_64."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:368
msgid ""
":gh:`2642`: :func:`cpu_freq` returned values ~1000x too small on Apple M4+, "
"and failed on M5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:370
msgid ""
":gh:`2726`: :meth:`Process.num_ctx_switches` returned an unusually high "
"number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:372
msgid ""
":gh:`2841`: :func:`cpu_freq` could raise :exc:`SystemError` when frequency "
"data is missing (e.g. Apple M5). It now returns ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:374
msgid ""
":gh:`2853`: :func:`memory_physical` and :func:`memory_swap` could "
"raise :exc:`RuntimeError` (``(ipc/mig) array not large enough``) on newer "
"macOS versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:377
msgid ""
":gh:`2854`: :meth:`Process.cmdline` and :meth:`Process.environ` could "
"raise :exc:`SystemError` instead of :exc:`AccessDenied`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:379
msgid ""
":gh:`3115`: :func:`cpu_stats` returned memory page counts instead of CPU "
"statistics. All fields are now ``0``, since macOS doesn't keep these "
"counters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:382
msgid ""
":gh:`3117`: :func:`memory_swap` :field:`sin` and :field:`sout` counted all "
"page-ins and page-outs, including file-backed ones, instead of swap-ins and "
"swap-outs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:386
msgid "**Bug fixes: BSD**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:388
msgid ""
":gh:`2744`, [NetBSD], :label:`critical`: fix possible double ``free()`` "
"in :func:`memory_swap`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:390
msgid ""
":gh:`2848`, :label:`critical`: :func:`net_io_counters` could overflow a "
"stack buffer on unusually long interface names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:392
msgid ""
":gh:`3071`, [OpenBSD], :label:`critical`: :func:`users` crashed if ``/var/"
"run/utmp`` could not be opened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:394
msgid ""
":gh:`3073`, [NetBSD], :label:`critical`: :func:`net_connections` "
"and :meth:`Process.net_connections` read freed memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:396
msgid ""
":gh:`1534`, [NetBSD]: :meth:`Process.exe` is now read via ``sysctl()`` "
"instead of the ``/proc/pid/exe`` symlink."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:398
msgid ""
":gh:`1801`, [FreeBSD]: :func:`cpu_freq` could "
"raise :exc:`UnicodeDecodeError` on non-UTF-8 ``dev.cpu.N.freq_levels`` data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:400
msgid ""
":gh:`2746`, [FreeBSD]: :meth:`Process.memory_maps` :field:`rss` "
"and :field:`private` were in pages instead of bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:402
msgid ""
":gh:`2782`, [FreeBSD]: :func:`cpu_count` (``logical=False``) returned "
"``None`` on systems without hyper-threading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:404
msgid ""
":gh:`2791`, [FreeBSD]: ``sysctl()`` calls failed if the kernel returned "
"fewer bytes than the buffer size (normal for variable-length data)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:406
msgid ""
":gh:`2795`, [FreeBSD]: :func:`cpu_freq` could raise :exc:`RuntimeError` "
"(``size mismatch``) on some systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:408
msgid ""
":gh:`2811`, :gh:`2813`, [OpenBSD]: :func:`memory_physical` :field:`shared` "
"was in pages instead of bytes, and overvalued. :field:`buffers` was always "
"0; it now equals :field:`cached`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:411
msgid ""
":gh:`2814`, :gh:`2815`, [NetBSD]: :func:`memory_physical` :field:`cached` "
"(included anonymous pages) and :field:`shared` were overvalued."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:413
msgid ""
":gh:`2822`: :meth:`Process.cmdline` on NetBSD could raise ``OSError: [Errno "
"14] Bad address`` instead of :exc:`NoSuchProcess` for an exiting process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:416
msgid ""
":gh:`2888`, [FreeBSD], [OpenBSD]: :class:`Process` methods could wrongly "
"raise :exc:`NoSuchProcess` (\"PID has been reused\") after a system clock "
"update (e.g. NTP). The PID reuse check is now disabled there (and on SunOS "
"and AIX)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:420
msgid ""
":gh:`2902`, [NetBSD], [OpenBSD]: :meth:`Process.cmdline` could raise "
"``OSError(EINVAL)`` (OpenBSD) or a broken :exc:`NoSuchProcess` (NetBSD) for "
"a process which died mid-call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:423
msgid ""
":gh:`2903`: :meth:`Process.nice` could raise :exc:`NoSuchProcess` for "
"processes in ``SIDL`` state (not fully initialized)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:425
msgid ""
":gh:`2905`, [FreeBSD], [OpenBSD], "
"[NetBSD]: :meth:`Process.gids` :field:`saved` reported the saved *user* ID "
"instead of the group ID (since 2011)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:428
msgid ""
":gh:`2907`, [NetBSD]: exiting processes (not yet zombies) weren't "
"recognized: :class:`Process` methods raised :exc:`NoSuchProcess` instead "
"of :exc:`ZombieProcess`, and :meth:`Process.status` returned "
"``\"sleeping\"`` or ``\"?\"``. :data:`STATUS_SUSPENDED` was never "
"returned. :meth:`Process.environ` raised :exc:`OSError` for exiting or "
"zombie processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:433
msgid ""
":gh:`2929`, [NetBSD], [OpenBSD]: :meth:`Process.num_fds` returned a wrong, "
"system-wide number, and :meth:`Process.open_files` always returned an empty "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:436
msgid ""
":gh:`2951`, [OpenBSD]: :func:`cpu_times` returned times averaged across CPUs "
"instead of summed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:438
msgid ""
":gh:`2952`, [OpenBSD]: :meth:`Process.environ` raised ``OSError(EINVAL)`` "
"for an exiting process. For a zombie it now raises :exc:`ZombieProcess` on "
"all BSDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:441
msgid ""
":gh:`3016`, [NetBSD]: :meth:`Process.num_fds` and :meth:`Process.open_files` "
"for PID 0 returned the file descriptors of every process on the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:443
msgid ""
":gh:`3020`, [FreeBSD]: :meth:`Process.memory_maps` now brackets non-file "
"mapping names, e.g. ``[sys:vm_anon]`` instead of ``sys:vm_anon``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:445
msgid ":gh:`3013`: :func:`net_io_counters` returned garbage on 32-bit builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:446
msgid ""
":gh:`3032`, [FreeBSD]: :func:`cpu_stats` counters wrapped around at 2^32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:447
msgid ""
":gh:`3017`, [FreeBSD]: :func:`pid_exists` returned ``False`` for PID 0 (the "
"kernel), even though :func:`pids` lists it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:449
msgid ""
":gh:`3072`, [OpenBSD]: :func:`users` could return trailing garbage "
"in :field:`name`, :field:`terminal` or :field:`host`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:451
msgid ""
":gh:`3116`, [OpenBSD], [NetBSD]: :meth:`Process.cpu_times` returned the "
"children's user + system time in both :field:`children_user` "
"and :field:`children_system`, counting it twice. Same "
"for :meth:`Process.threads` :field:`user_time` and :field:`system_time` on "
"NetBSD. The total now goes in the user field, and the system field is ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:457
msgid "**Bug fixes: POSIX**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:459
msgid ""
":gh:`2877`, :label:`critical`: fix a one-byte stack buffer overflow "
"in :func:`users` when ``ut_host`` filled the whole field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:461
msgid ""
":gh:`3070`, :label:`critical`: :func:`net_if_addrs` freed an uninitialized "
"pointer if ``getifaddrs()`` failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:463
msgid ""
":gh:`3075`, [SunOS], :label:`critical`: :meth:`Process.memory_maps` could "
"read past the end of a heap buffer if reading ``/proc/[pid]/xmap`` failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:465
msgid ""
":gh:`2789`, [AIX], :label:`build-fail`: compilation failed because of a typo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:466
msgid ""
":gh:`2858`, [SunOS], :label:`memleak`: :func:`disk_io_counters` leaked the "
"result dict when ``kstat_read()`` failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:468
msgid ""
":gh:`2687`, [SunOS]: :func:`users` failed with ``ValueError`` on illumos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:469
msgid ""
":gh:`3074`, [SunOS]: :meth:`Process.terminal` returned the path of file "
"descriptor 0 instead of ``None`` for processes without a controlling "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:472
msgid ""
":gh:`3076`, [SunOS]: :meth:`Process.cmdline` and :meth:`Process.environ` "
"could raise ``SystemError`` instead of :exc:`NoSuchProcess` if the process "
"exited mid-read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:475
msgid ""
":gh:`2778`: :func:`net_if_addrs` skipped interfaces with no addresses (e.g. "
"tunnels), unlike :func:`net_io_counters` and :func:`net_if_stats`. They are "
"now included, with :field:`family` set to :data:`socket.AF_UNSPEC`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:478
msgid ""
":gh:`2964`: :func:`net_if_addrs` returned the interface's own address "
"as :field:`broadcast` for ``/32`` IPv4 addresses. It now returns ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:480
msgid ""
":gh:`2953`, [SunOS]: :meth:`Process.gids` returned a ``puids`` named "
"tuple, :meth:`Process.nice` was off by +20, "
"and :meth:`Process.net_connections` returned UNIX sockets with ``type=-1`` / "
"``fd=-1`` and raised ``RuntimeError`` for zombies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:484
msgid ""
":gh:`3015`: :meth:`Process.nice` on PID 0 changed the niceness of the "
"calling process (on macOS and AIX the getter returned the caller's). It now "
"raises :exc:`AccessDenied`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:487
msgid ""
":gh:`3017`: :exc:`OSError` messages could raise :exc:`UnicodeDecodeError` in "
"non-UTF-8 locales."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:489
msgid ""
":gh:`3018`, [SunOS], [AIX]: :func:`boot_time`, and :func:`cpu_times` per-CPU "
"values on SunOS, lost precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:491
msgid ""
":gh:`3013`, [AIX]: :meth:`Process.uids` and :meth:`Process.gids` returned "
"garbage on 32-bit builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:493
msgid ""
":gh:`3013`, [SunOS]: :meth:`Process.uids` and :meth:`Process.gids` returned "
"negative numbers for ephemeral ids (>= 2**31, e.g. SMB and NFSv4 identities)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:497
msgid "7.2.2 — 2026-01-28"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:501
msgid ""
":gh:`2705`, [Linux], [macOS], [BSD]: :meth:`Process.wait` no longer uses a "
"busy loop. It now uses ``pidfd_open()`` + ``poll()`` on Linux (requires "
"Linux >= 5.3 and Python >= 3.9), and ``kqueue()`` on macOS and BSD."
msgstr ""

